# Polish round 4, part 1 (0.0.5j): a repeating reminder, the task-button
# menu, Ctrl+L, Settings scrolling at a small window height, and the
# launcher's two-press power off. 1280x800.
gui: desktop up at 1280x800
cerberus kernel shell
# A daily reminder appears in the calendar's list with "(daily)".
!mouseto 1200 770
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!key daily 07:30 Stand up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol2-1.png
!mouseto 120 400
!button left down
!button left up
!key cat /data/reminders.txt
!wait 0.5
# (no data disk here: the file does not exist; the reminder lives in memory)
!key clear
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol2-2.png
!key ticks
!wait 0.5
ticks=
# Right-click the Terminal's taskbar button (x=445..620, y=770): Minimise is
# the second item; the terminal goes; then "ticks" typed goes nowhere, so
# restore it through the same menu's first item.
!mouseto 530 770
!button right down
!button right up
!wait 0.4
!screenshot build/qol2-3.png
!mouseto 560 596
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!screenshot build/qol2-4.png
!mouseto 530 770
!button right down
!button right up
!wait 0.4
!mouseto 560 564
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!key ticks
!wait 0.5
ticks=
# Power off needs two presses: one press only arms it.
!mouseto 28 780
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 0.5
!mouseto 274 710
!button left down
!button left up
!screenshot build/qol2-5.png
!button left down
!button left up
!wait 3
gui: power off requested from the launcher
!poweredoff
